.Dd June 28, 2026
.Dt proxy_helper 8
.Os Linux
.Sh NAME
.Nm proxy_helper
.Nd helper for constructing proxy environment variables from system settings
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c | Fl s | Fl f | Fl w
.Op Fl p | Fl -pac Ar path_or_url
.Op Fl u | Fl -url Ar url
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads the proxy settings from Linux system settings (GNOME, KDE)
or local configuration files, and configures the
.Ev http_proxy ,
.Ev https_proxy ,
.Ev ftp_proxy
and
.Ev no_proxy
environment variables.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c | Fl -csh
Generate C-shell commands on stdout.  This is the default if
.Ev SHELL
ends with "csh".
.It Fl s | Fl -sh
Generate Bourne shell commands on stdout.  This is the default if
.Ev SHELL
does not match csh, fish, or powershell.
.It Fl f | Fl -fish
Generate Fish shell commands on stdout.  This is the default if
.Ev SHELL
ends with "fish".
.It Fl w | Fl -powershell
Generate PowerShell commands on stdout.  This is the default if
.Ev SHELL
ends with "pwsh" or "powershell".
.It Fl p | Fl -pac Ar path_or_url
Enable Proxy Auto-Configuration (PAC) script evaluation using a custom PAC file
path or URL. If omitted, proxy_helper automatically retrieves the active PAC
URL from system configurations.
.It Fl u | Fl -url Ar url
The target URL used for PAC script evaluation (default: "www.google.com").
.El
.Pp
The
.Ev no_proxy
variable is generated based on the rules below:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -offset indent -compact
.It
If a host matches the pattern \fI*.some.domain.name\fP, then \fIsome.domain.name\fP is added.
.It
If a host matches a valid IPv4 address, then the host is added as is.
.It
If a host matches a valid IPv6 address, then the host is added after removing square brackets (e.g., \fIfe80::1\fP).
.It
If a host matches a valid CIDR subnet notation (IPv4 or IPv6), then the host is added as is (e.g., \fI192.168.1.0/24\fP or \fIfe80::/64\fP).
.It
Ignored otherwise.
.El
.Pp
The proxy settings are resolved in the following priority order:
  1. Environment variable override: PROXY_HELPER_PAC_URL
  2. User configuration file: ~/.config/proxy_helper/config.toml
  3. System-wide configuration file: /etc/proxy_helper/config.toml
  4. GNOME desktop proxy settings (via gsettings)
  5. KDE desktop proxy settings (via kioslaverc)
.Sh USAGE
The
.Nm 
utility should not be invoked directly.
It is intended only for use by the shell profile.
.Pp
In your
.I /etc/profile
for Bash, or
.I /etc/zprofile
for Zsh, add the following code snippet:
.Pp
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if [ -x /usr/local/libexec/proxy_helper ]; then
    eval `/usr/local/libexec/proxy_helper -s`
fi
.Ed
.Pp
In your
.I ~/.config/fish/config.fish
for Fish, add the following code snippet:
.Pp
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if test -x /usr/local/libexec/proxy_helper
    eval (/usr/local/libexec/proxy_helper -f)
end
.Ed
.Pp
In your profile script for PowerShell, add the following code snippet:
.Pp
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if (Test-Path /usr/local/libexec/proxy_helper) {
    /usr/local/libexec/proxy_helper -w | Invoke-Expression
}
.Ed
.Sh AUTHOR
Takuma WATANABE
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr path_helper 8
